WEBVTT

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:18.910
Looking down from two miles above the surface of the earth, it's impossible not to be impressed

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:25.110
by the sheer grandeur and splendor and power of the natural world.

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:29.970
Ten years ago in the...

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.050
In a television series called Planet Earth, we revealed many of those wonders, but today

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:37.990
much has changed.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:50.880
We can now show life on our planet in entirely new ways, closer to animals than ever before,

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:59.070
and reveal new wildlife dramas the very first time.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:04.420
That's not all.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:07.800
Our planet has changed too.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:14.360
Never have those wildernesses been as fragile and as precious as they are today.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:21.080
At this crucial time for the natural world,

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:24.370
we will journey to every corner of the globe

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:29.320
for the greatest treasures of our living planet.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:41.260
and reveal the extreme lengths animals go to to survive.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:09.660
our cities to see how life is adapting to the newest habitat on earth. This is

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:11.180
planet Earth 2.

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:59.890
of thes of islands, each one a world in minutes.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.730
a microcosm of our living planet.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:09.470
The struggles to survive on these remote lands

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:14.060
reflect the challenges faced by all life on Earth.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:29.360
The island of Escudo off the coast of Panama.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:35.890
Home to the pygmy, three-toed sloth.

