Isolated on a speck of land no bigger than New York's Central Park the size of an island has a huge influence

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.080
on the fate of those cast away there,

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:11.940
the island of Komodo in Indonesia.

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:53.340
long and weighing an impressive 150 pounds. These are the largest living lizards on the planet.

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:17.920
It's unusual to find large predators on islands, yet for four million years the Komodo dragon has dominated here.

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:29.970
It might seem there wouldn't be...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:38.520
enough food to support such giants on this relatively small island, but reptiles being

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:50.330
cold-blooded mean only about a tenth of the food a carnivorous mammal would. A single meal will last

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:59.970
a dragon a month. They're so successful that their only serious competition comes...

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.850
from others of their own kind, and there are some 2,000 of them here.

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:33.330
This giant, however, isn't looking for food.

00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:35.770
He's looking for a mate.

00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:43.740
Female dragons come into season only once a year.

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:55.780
She's receptive.

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:06.870
So far, so good.

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:14.240
But he strayed into someone else's patch.

00:10:20.860 --> 00:10:24.940
Another cute male thinks he is the king here.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.740
Space being limited on islands, dragon territories overlap,

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:38.130
and that creates continual conflict.

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:49.200
In dragon society, size is everything.

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:10.020
But if rivals are closely matched, the outcome can be uncertain.

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:21.380
Muscular tails strike with the power of sledgehammers.

00:11:32.140 --> 00:11:36.000
...and their serrated teeth are as sharp as steak knives.

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:50.450
... tries to topple his opponent.

00:12:13.950 --> 00:12:19.570
The most powerful dragons win the right to mate.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:35.540
Food and space on the small islands can often lead to intense competition.

00:12:37.510 --> 00:12:42.860
But some islands are immense, more like miniature continents,

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:49.510
and these provide opportunities for life to experiment and evolve.

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:59.980
Madagascar is one of the biggest islands, and also one of the oldest islands.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:05.450
having split away from Africa over 120 million years ago.

00:13:17.410 --> 00:13:18.890
With time and isolation,

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:23.730
its animals have adapted to take advantage of every available niche.

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:35.730
The island now has some 250,000 different species,

00:13:36.280 --> 00:13:38.840
most found nowhere else on Earth.

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:54.660
These are not monkeys, but lemurs.

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:04.940
From a single ancestor, about a hundred different types have evolved.

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:14.900
The largest, the Indri, seldom comes down from the branches.

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:27.110
The much smaller ringtails wander in troops across the forest floor,

00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:28.390
searching for fruit.

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:34.650
and tiny bamboo lemurs eat nothing except bamboo.

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:46.060
With few competitors, lemurs have been free

00:14:46.060 --> 00:14:49.360
to colonize almost every environment on the island,

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:54.620
even the most extreme.

00:15:02.780 --> 00:15:07.120
This baby Shifaka has a hard life ahead of it.

00:15:12.190 --> 00:15:17.430
He's been born in the most arid and hostile corner of Madagascar's vast landscape.

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:24.120
If he is to survive here, he has much to learn.

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:34.300
The spiny forest is like a desert.

00:15:35.970 --> 00:15:40.810
It rarely rains, so water and food is very hard to find.

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:52.590
Moving from tree to tree is a perilous business.

00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:58.800
Here, nearly all the plants are covered with ferocious spines.

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:04.700
His mother searches the treetops for the youngest leaves.

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:11.240
They provide the only food and water to sustain the family.

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:21.920
At three months old, the youngster is starting to explore.

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:29.970
All too soon, he will have to...

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:31.580
fend for himself up here,

00:16:37.650 --> 00:16:41.780
but it's altogether easier to stay on mother's back.

00:16:42.340 --> 00:16:53.130
If he can master the strange ways of this forest,

00:16:54.470 --> 00:16:57.290
he will have a little corner of Madagascar to himself.

00:17:04.760 --> 00:17:07.960
Island life encourages animals to do things differently.

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:12.870
